{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"elfin-decagonal-polarbear","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Mirror inventory finding F11 (reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md), LOW.\n\n- src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py ROUTES (78 live route names)\n- src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py:22 _CROSS_SESSION_WARN_COMMANDS — 14 hardcoded spellings, used at :74\n\nAll 14 are live route names today, so this is preventive.\n\nScope note from the sweep: WHICH verbs warn cross-session is a DISTINCT CONCEPT (a predicate subset,\nthe same rule that makes _NOT_CLAIMABLE_STATUSES not a mirror). The mirror is only the SPELLINGS,\nwhich must match route names with nothing enforcing it. It is the one CLI policy subset not folded\ninto derive_policy_sets (_registry.py:680), so a route rename silently drops the warning.\n\nProposed fix: add-route-flag — a warn_cross_session flag on Route, folded into derive_policy_sets.","id":"1daf-a435-2387-412c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Validate _CROSS_SESSION_WARN_COMMANDS spellings against ROUTES, or add a route flag (mirror F11)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788317703158884001,"uuid":"6db3cf1d-ecda-4976-8b6a-5551c200e2e2"}